# TypeScript

## Naming

| Kind | Convention | Example |
|------|------------|---------|
| Files | kebab-case | `parallax-section.tsx` |
| Components | PascalCase | `ParallaxSection` |
| Functions/vars | camelCase | `sanityFetch` |
| Types | PascalCase | `ProjectProps` |
| Workspace packages | kebab-case | `@repo/cms` |

## Types

- Prefer `type` for props and simple unions; `interface` when extending is needed.
- Import types with `import type { ... }`.
- No `any` — use `unknown` + narrowing, or generated Sanity types.
- After CMS changes, use `pnpm cms:typegen` types instead of manual casts.

## React props

```ts
type ParallaxSectionProps = {
  children: ReactNode
  className?: string
}

export function ParallaxSection({ children, className }: ParallaxSectionProps) {
```

## Config inheritance

Apps extend `@repo/tsconfig/nextjs.json`. Shared base in `packages/tsconfig/base.json`.

## Strictness

`strict: true` everywhere. Do not disable strict checks to pass builds.
